{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.EndSemisimpleGeneral","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.EndSemisimpleGeneral","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MatrixSemisimple","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.SimpleModule.WedderburnArtin"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.EndSemisimpleGeneral.instIsSemisimpleRing_end_of_isSemisimpleModule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.EndSemisimpleGeneral.instIsSemisimpleRing_end_of_isSemisimpleModule","kind":"instance","line":6,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/EndSemisimpleGeneral.lean#L6-L38","doc":"**`IsSemisimpleRing (Module.End R M)` for any finite semisimple module** —\nMathlib's `proof_wanted IsSemisimpleRing.module_end`, in full.\n\n`MathlibExt.EndSemisimple.isSemisimpleRing_end` covers `M` a\nfinite-dimensional vector space over a **field**. This is the general\nstatement, with the same hypotheses the `proof_wanted` carries.\n\nThree steps, each already available:\n\n1. `IsSemisimpleModule.exists_end_ringEquiv` decomposes\n   `End R M ≃+* Π i, Matrix (Fin dᵢ) (Fin dᵢ) (End R Sᵢ)` with each `Sᵢ` a\n   **simple** submodule — this is the isotypic decomposition, and it is where\n   `Module.Finite` is used;\n2. Schur's lemma (`Module.End.instDivisionRing`) makes each `End R Sᵢ` a\n   division ring, so each block is semisimple by\n   `MatrixSemisimple.instIsSemisimpleRing_matrix`;\n3. a finite product of semisimple rings is semisimple, and\n   `RingEquiv.isSemisimpleRing` transports back.\n\nNote this does **not** need the general-base matrix result: the blocks land on\ndivision rings by Schur, which is precisely the case already proved. ","signatureChunk":0}]}